variantes.contenu_markdown:
```
procedure swap(var p, q : integer);
var tmp : integer;
begin
  tmp := p; p := q; q := tmp
end;                          { call: swap(m, n) }
```

```
void swap(int *p, int *q)
{
    int tmp = *p;
    *p = *q;
    *q = tmp;
}
/* call: swap(&m, &n); */
```

These are examples of logic: no Pascal or C compiler was used. Their logic was checked by an executed Python translation: with m = 7 and n = 2, the reference version gives m = 2 and n = 7, while a by-value version leaves m = 7 and n = 2.

